                Stigma - You can feel it the moment you step in here, can't you? That quiet question everyone carries: "What am I, really, when it matters?" That question introduces instability. So we remove it.:
                Poise - You don't remove doubt. You replace it with something simpler.:
                Moxie - "Liability." "Essential." "Dead weight." You're not removing uncertainty-you're handing out conclusions before anything even happens.:
                Rapture - Yeah, but that's the fun part, right? Watching it play out anyway.:
                Scalpel - Hesitation confirmed.:
                Kaera - Stop- You didn't even give them a chance to respond!:
                Scalpel - The hesitation was the response. It aligned with the classification. Correction was therefore appropriate.:
                Poise - You're acting like you observed something. But you already decided what that hesitation meant before it happened.:
                Sable - You're not just labeling them. You're shaping how they see themselves before they even act. That's not evaluation-that's influence.:
                Stigma - Of course it is. People are far easier to understand once they've accepted a role.:
                Rapture - You don't find out who someone is by talking about it. You find out when something pushes back hard enough that they stop pretending.:
                Bragg - He's not completely wrong. When it's real-when it's actually dangerous-you fall back on what you are.:
                Chock - No. You fall back on training. Discipline. Habit. That's not the same thing as identity.:
                Stigma - Let's simplify this. You see someone hurt, and you help them. Again. And again. So tell me- what are you without that?:
                Kaera - No. I've chosen. That's different.:
                Kade - This isn't discovery. You set the criteria, you control the environment, you define the outcomes... and then you call what survives "truth.":
                Kaera - You're not revealing anything. You're stripping people down until the only thing left is what your system can recognize.:
                Kade - It's not identity. It's filtration.:
                Rapture - Then let's find out what survives when we apply a little more pressure.:
                EVENT - award_task - Meet scalpel

