                Scalpel - Oh, I'm counting on it. The hesitation was the response. It aligned with the classification. Correction was therefore appropriate.:
                Poise - You're acting like you observed something. But you already decided what that hesitation meant before it happened.:
                Sable - You're not just labeling them. You're shaping how they see themselves before they even act. That's not evaluation-that's influence.:
                Scalpel - Of course it is. People are far easier to understand once they've accepted a role.:
                Rapture - You don't find out who someone is by talking about it. You find out when something pushes back hard enough that they stop pretending.:
